WEBVTT

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.360
Whoa...

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.490
Look at all of 'em.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:17.950
It's like a gathering of armies 
from around the Holy See.

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:24.580
<i>This whole place feels on edge.</i>

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:29.880
<i>The battlefield smell that's so familiar...</i>

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.890
<b><i>City of Humans</i></b>

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:42.640
Hold it, girl.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.290
Do you mean me?

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:46.270
What is that outfit?

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.690
Teacher?!

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:50.270
I forgot...

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:53.150
This is a fortress of the Holy See.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:56.280
You cannot enter with 
such outrageous clothing!

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.660
Sir, this costume is for our troupe...

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.200
A traveling troupe?

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.450
But that doesn't excuse it!

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:10.030
Come, let us go.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:13.670
Are you really sure that was a good idea?

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:15.970
She's obviously a witch.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:17.800
Everyone is staring, right?

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:18.840
Come with me!

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.010
What?

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.680
That outfit's a bad idea.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.060
You need to buy some normal clothes.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.390
This is normal for me.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:29.400
Why are you being so stubborn?

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:34.190
Schierke!

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:37.820
Sorry...

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:39.530
You're mean.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:41.660
Who cares about your stupid hat?

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.790
It's your fault for not listening!

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:47.810
Idiot!

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:50.040
If you wander around in that stuff...

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:53.460
Jeez, what is that witch thinking?

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.920
Hey, Droppy! What the hell?!

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.430
It's "Dropey," Ivalera.

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:01.930
Those robes and hat were handmade by Flora.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:04.180
Everything else she had burned!

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:05.810
Handmade?

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:07.890
They're all she has left!

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.190
You really are a monkey, making a girl cry!

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:13.480
Schierke, wait!

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.320
Isidoro...

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.700
We'll find an inn.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:20.820
Go bring her back.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:23.950
I'll go with you.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:25.910
Schierke!

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.080
Hey, hello?

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.670
Where are you going?

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.120
Somewhere without anyone else.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.350
What is that?

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.930
Wait, what the hell are you?

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.290
That is his body.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.210
Schierke!

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:13.830
Move away for a second.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.920
Schierke, what happened?

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:24.760
It hurts! It hurts!

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.630
Let me down... Let me down!

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:31.520
Release me...

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.450
Who are you?

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:38.360
What offense caused these 
people to be hanged here?

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:41.610
This isn't a place for kids.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:45.490
Well, I guess it's okay...

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:48.240
These are Kushans.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:50.290
Well, Kushans or not,

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:53.250
they were slaves that resided in Vritannis.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:54.750
Slaves...

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.880
Vritannis is a merchant city.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:03.130
To other nations in the Holy See, 
Kushans are religious enemies.

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:04.760
But here, they're more.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.510
They're a product.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:09.060
But with this huge war,

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:12.310
we can't keep doing that, anymore.

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:18.360
Since Vritannis has been honored
by becoming a Holy See naval base.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:22.900
So the city hanged them, 
as sacrifices to morale.

00:04:23.610 --> 00:04:25.160
<i>That's the reason?</i>

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:29.950
<i>People will take each other's 
lives for such a reason?</i>

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:34.750
Displaying the bodies of the 
dead is a desecration.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.710
It is not to be allowed.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:39.250
Now I shall take them down to cremate.

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:41.260
You will help me.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:42.760
Understood?

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:04.990
Hey, Schierke... Let's go back.

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:06.450
The sun's setting!

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:07.820
Come on...

00:05:18.670 --> 00:05:22.550
You'd need more than a forest's 
worth of trees to build all these!

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:25.720
<i>What are they trying to do,</i>

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:29.510
<i>making something so large?</i>

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:32.040
<i>So many people and things,</i>

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.730
<i>gathered merely for bloodshed?</i>

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:39.690
<i>This is the world to which they belong.</i>

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:50.760
<i>Mistress, the voices of the spirits 
are very hard to hear here,</i>

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:54.450
<i>drowned out by human voices.</i>

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.250
The wharf? You're sure?

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.120
Yeah.

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:01.000
You with her? Then, you should hurry.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.920
That place isn't safe after dark.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:06.380
Armed merchant ships, basically pirates,

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:07.800
weigh anchor there.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:11.180
She could be kidnapped and 
sold to a foreign country...

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:12.350
Wait!

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:15.470
Are you looking for the witch?

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.150
I'm searching for someone.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:24.570
If you know something about the 
witch, would you tell me?

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:28.200
Why is someone like you looking for a witch?

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:29.860
I know!

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.700
You plan to catch and hand 
her over to the government,

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.580
so you can get the glory!

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:35.200
Glory?

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.580
Don't try and fool me!

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:40.620
The way you're dressed, you're some 
noble's son, squiring for a knight!

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:44.250
You want glory, so you get 
promoted to full knighthood.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:45.210
That's so petty!

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:46.590
Hey...

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:47.970
I'll stop you!

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:52.340
Wait! Listen to me!

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:02.650
Schierke, I'm hungry.

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:03.730
Let's go back.

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:05.690
Wow!

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:09.950
So witches are real, huh?

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.000
You're a witch, right?

00:07:19.970 --> 00:07:22.000
Do I look like one?

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:24.080
Yep.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.460
You have a staff and pointy hat.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:28.420
And you talk to animals.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:30.470
Also, there's her.

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:34.180
A girl accompanied by a fairy 
could only be a witch.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:36.640
You can see me.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:37.890
<i>She is...</i>

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:40.310
And then, your actions back there.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.600
The Kushans that were hung up,

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:45.810
you released them, didn't you?

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.820
You were able to see that?

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:50.280
It was really cool,

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:52.610
the way you bossed those grown-ups around!

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:54.200
Was that magic?

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:56.990
It wasn't anything that special...

00:07:57.330 --> 00:08:01.540
But don't witches live in the 
mountains or forests?

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:03.250
What are you doing here?

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:05.250
I'm on a journey.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.420
Alone?

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:09.170
Or with her, just you two?

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:10.590
No.

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:14.050
Ever since we came to this 
city, a lot has happened.

00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:19.180
It's pretty hard, isn't it?

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:21.390
Being different than others.

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:24.900
Are you from this city?

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:25.600
Nope.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:28.230
A lot has happened to me, as well.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:30.190
Let's say, hypothetically...

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.990
There was an ugly duckling.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:33.780
Duckling?

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.950
Oh, I know that fairytale!

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:40.120
The ugly duckling was different from everyone, so she was left out.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:42.200
Because the ugly duckling was...

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.660
A swan!

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:45.000
A black kite!

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:50.090
One day a murder of mean crows 
attacked the duck's nest.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:54.220
The weak ducklings couldn't fly away,

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.760
and they were all captured.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:00.930
The black kite was convinced she 
was just a weird duckling,

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:02.640
and didn't know how to fly.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:03.930
So she was also captured.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:09.320
But then, it was the king 
of birds who saved them.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:11.070
The white hawk.

00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:12.900
Hawk?

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:16.570
The white hawk brought 
dragons in his service,

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:19.700
and they quickly defeated the crows.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.790
Black kites and hawks are 
related to one another.

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:25.910
For the first time, the young 
black kite met someone similar,

00:09:25.910 --> 00:09:28.210
and she realized she could fly.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:29.420
And then what happened?

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:30.710
The white hawk

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:34.670
defeated the crows that were
rampaging through the country.

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:39.420
Not only were there dragons by its side, 
but there were ducklings,

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:42.840
and even stray crows that had turned to good.

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:45.170
The black kite was special.

00:09:45.170 --> 00:09:48.650
Only she could fly in the same 
sky as the white hawk.

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:50.860
Only she could feel the same wind.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:54.990
What a romantic situation!

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:58.030
But then, one day...

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:01.780
The duckling princess, whom the 
king of crows had captured,

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:03.990
was saved by the white hawk.

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:09.880
The cowardly ducklings wanted to 
marry her to the white hawk,

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:13.630
to strengthen their bond 
to the powerful hawk.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:15.170
Oh, my!

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:17.970
The black kite disliked this.

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:24.180
So she tried to make herself feel 
better by looking at the sea.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:25.680
And then? And then?

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:28.640
The black kite met a young 
owl from the forest,

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:30.850
who was surrounded by gulls.

00:10:31.770 --> 00:10:33.690
The black kite thought to herself

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:37.780
that even though the young owl 
was surrounded by many gulls,

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:40.110
she looked a bit lonely...

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:43.660
"We're kind of similar.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:49.420
I wonder if we can be friends," she thought.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:52.130
The—

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:56.800
The owl felt the same way...

00:10:59.130 --> 00:11:03.850
Hey, do you have someone 
who understands you?

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:07.350
Everyone I travel with is normal,

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:09.100
so when it comes to witches...

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:16.610
<i>They're in harmony.</i>

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:17.690
It's love, isn't it?

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:18.610
It's love!

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.610
I-It isn't like that!

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:24.240
Just, as a grown-up, he's been 
watching out for me.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:27.750
And so, I find myself letting him spoil me.

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.790
Stop right there, brats!

00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:36.460
Who are they?

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:37.920
Slavers? Pirates?

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:38.630
Those are...

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.180
You won't get away!

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:44.140
You wanna make it hard, huh?

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.850
Stop crying!

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:49.730
There's no place to run, anyway!

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:51.270
Stop this at once.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:58.650
Do not make me witness 
further ugliness today.

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:08.320
Girl, you think you're a witch
or something, dressed like that?

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:09.620
I do.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:12.410
And you are pirates, aren't you?

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:12.410
Pirates!

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:15.290
You plan to kidnap those kids and sell them!

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:18.960
These are Kushan kids, 
whose parents were hanged!

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:23.960
That's why we can't leave them in the city.

00:12:24.320 --> 00:12:27.720
My, maybe this place deserves 
to be put to the torch.

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:33.170
To a witch such as I, 
city law and merchant logic mean nothing.

00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:37.100
Girl, if you talk back to us, you'll join—

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:39.100
Huh?

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:40.770
Hey, what's wrong?

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:43.360
I... I can't move!

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:44.690
Amazing.

00:12:44.690 --> 00:12:46.530
Magic? Was that magic?

00:12:46.530 --> 00:12:48.120
J-Just a hypnotic suggestion!

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:50.610
What did you do, girl?!

00:12:50.610 --> 00:12:52.780
If you don't let me move again, I'll beat—

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:54.450
What?

00:12:56.160 --> 00:12:58.460
I knew this was going to happen...

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:00.170
Isidoro?

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:01.750
Is that the one?

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:02.710
Definitely not.

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:04.170
Hey, pirates!

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:06.010
Enough of your crimes!

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:09.720
Don't try and say you're gathering 
these kids for a picnic!

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:10.970
Pathetic!

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:13.180
You stupid brat!

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:19.230
<i>I did that without thinking.</i>

00:13:24.190 --> 00:13:27.780
<i>It's the first time I've cut someone down...</i>

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:31.450
Now that we've seen our friend's blood...

00:13:31.780 --> 00:13:32.950
Isidoro!

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:35.240
Girl, stay out of this,

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:37.160
unless you wanna get hurt.

00:13:38.910 --> 00:13:40.330
<i>At this rate...</i>

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:44.250
<i>Stop. Don't use that.</i>

00:13:44.250 --> 00:13:47.130
<i>Wait... Why are you so mad?</i>

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:48.130
That isn't it.

00:13:48.130 --> 00:13:50.510
He wants to conceal what you are.

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:52.380
Isn't that nice of him?

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:54.930
You can do it, monkey!

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:55.510
<i>She can hear our telepathic conversation?</i>

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:04.690
Wow! Wow!

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:05.770
He's fighting grown-ups!

00:14:05.770 --> 00:14:08.410
But eventually, they'll catch him.

00:14:11.780 --> 00:14:14.240
All the inns are full...

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.240
Guts?

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:18.290
Throw down your weapon, 
and we won't kill you.

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:21.830
We'll just beat you half to death and 
hang you from the mast for a day...

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:29.960
What's your problem? 
Butt in and you'll get hurt.

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:31.840
Hey, there.

00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:36.100
Y-You're...

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:38.310
It seems you're helping my comrade.

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:39.600
I shall join you!

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.640
You wanna fight?

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:47.980
Wow...

00:14:47.980 --> 00:14:49.150
<i>He's...</i>

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:52.900
<i>He's slaughtering them without hesitation.</i>

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:08.000
That's the problem with kids.

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:14.050
Around adults, they don't know their place.

00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:15.760
Captain!

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:17.760
Definitely a pirate!

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:20.680
Listen up, kids.

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:23.930
The world of adults has stern rules.

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:28.770
And if you break them, you need 
to be punished a little.

00:15:28.770 --> 00:15:33.280
I thought pirates had more spine!

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:40.530
Not bad...

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:42.910
The standard swordsmanship of a noble.

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:44.080
But...

00:15:45.330 --> 00:15:46.170
Wait!

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:48.420
Take this.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:58.930
You shouldn't underestimate 
grown-ups, little boy.

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:02.100
Now, how will you pay for all this mess?

00:16:07.850 --> 00:16:09.270
Time for the main act...

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:10.900
The opener can get lost.

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:17.360
He's...

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:21.450
You can keep up with me on a ship?

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:22.660
<i>Of course.</i>

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:25.250
<i>I roll around, whenever I use my sword.</i>

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:27.730
<i>I can fight in any stance!</i>

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:30.630
<i>Oh, no!</i>

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:36.840
Your sword lacks the desire for bloodshed.

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:39.260
Now, enough games.

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:41.640
Men, tie them all up!

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:42.600
Yes, sir!

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:47.730
<i>Puck Spark!</i>

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:53.610
Now!

00:16:58.200 --> 00:16:59.850
The gate's closing!

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:03.700
Even if they're children, 
I don't know how we took

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:06.540
all these Kushans out of the 
city, with no problem.

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:08.580
What's going on?

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:10.620
That's...

00:17:10.620 --> 00:17:13.000
a secret! Right?

00:17:13.840 --> 00:17:17.210
Well? What will you do with the children?

00:17:17.210 --> 00:17:19.840
Take them with us, of course.

00:17:20.150 --> 00:17:21.720
You're being selfish again.

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:22.890
It's been settled.

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:24.970
This is my decision as a seer!

00:17:25.280 --> 00:17:27.730
Um, will that be all right?

00:17:28.010 --> 00:17:32.400
I don't want to ruin my fun memories.

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:36.570
And our boss isn't the kind of 
petty man to complain

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:38.820
about something like this, right?

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:40.030
Right?

00:17:40.780 --> 00:17:42.910
Fine. We'll take them.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:46.330
Take it.

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:47.660
What? Don't be stupid.

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:49.170
I can't take a stolen sword!

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:51.580
Can you protect them unarmed?

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:56.130
You're the one who dropped 
your sword in the sea, right?

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:58.880
How lame! Think you can 
be a knight like that?

00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:01.970
And you looked as stupid 
as a flipped-over frog!

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:05.640
And you staggered like a 
drunk on those boats!

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:06.350
Hey, witch girl...

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:09.850
Would you like to come with us?

00:18:13.430 --> 00:18:14.690
With...

00:18:18.290 --> 00:18:19.440
...you?

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:29.540
If you feel that you have 
no place in this world,

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:31.620
we would welcome you.

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:35.580
What will you do?

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:41.050
I...

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:47.390
I...

00:19:03.570 --> 00:19:05.700
Thank you, but...

00:19:06.490 --> 00:19:09.660
I have a place to go home to.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:11.830
I see...

00:19:12.870 --> 00:19:14.160
That man,

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:15.420
he's your...

00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:19.130
Tsk... Guess I got turned down.

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:20.170
Too bad.

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:22.170
I'm sorry.

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:25.220
Oh, right. I haven't gotten your name yet.

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:26.390
I'm Sonia.

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:27.760
I am Schierke.

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:28.970
Ivalera.

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:31.470
Whad's wong?

00:19:31.470 --> 00:19:34.770
Your pwetty hace is all veat up...

00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:39.860
You, too... I'd mistake you 
for a crushed meat bun.

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:41.820
Say fhat?!

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:46.200
Maybe I bweak awll your deeth?

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:49.200
Talk like a human being!

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:51.540
I'm Mule.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:52.870
What's your name?

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:54.580
Ijidodo.

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:57.710
I'll remember your name, Ijidodo!

00:19:57.710 --> 00:19:58.930
It's "Ijidodo"!

00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:00.340
Schierke...

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:03.840
Get away from this city, as soon as you can.

00:20:13.220 --> 00:20:14.310
What was that?

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:20.310
Let's meet again, forest owl!

00:20:21.980 --> 00:20:24.610
Okay, wet's head vack. 
The gate will ve cwosing.

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:28.590
He says, "Okay, let's head back. 
The gate will be closing."

00:20:30.530 --> 00:20:31.700
Um...

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:37.370
I'b swowwy boud your hat and cwothes...

00:20:37.570 --> 00:20:39.460
Huh? I couldn't hear you!

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:41.630
Speak a human language.

00:20:41.630 --> 00:20:45.010
I'm sorry about your hat and clothes...

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:48.630
And I'm sorry for being stubborn.

00:20:49.400 --> 00:20:51.970
Thank you for coming.

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:56.180
Not at all. We weren't able to help at all.

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:00.600
Okay, food time!

00:21:09.860 --> 00:21:13.080
It hurts, just looking at you.

00:21:14.030 --> 00:21:17.290
This place is filled with 
nasty sorts, isn't it?

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:19.830
Couldn't you find better lodgings?

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:21.380
It could not be helped.

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:23.750
The whole city is so full of soldiers,

00:21:23.750 --> 00:21:26.460
we should be grateful we found any place.

00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:29.170
Taverns are all the same.

00:21:29.170 --> 00:21:31.260
Gambling, fighting, whores.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:33.970
Come over here and pour me a drink, missy—

00:21:33.970 --> 00:21:35.310
Listen, mister...

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:38.230
And drunks.

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:41.870
Keep your feet off the table when we eat.

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:44.710
Everyone, we're back.

00:21:44.710 --> 00:21:45.430
Come on.

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:47.750
B-But...

00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:51.040
Ta-dah!

00:21:52.280 --> 00:21:54.180
The clothes make the witch, huh?

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:56.750
The tavern's owner

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:59.820
was nice enough to give us 
her daughter's old clothes.

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:03.760
It a little tight and hard to move in...

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:05.950
And I don't feel right without my staff.

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:08.260
It's only for while we stay in this city.

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:10.200
You look good.

00:22:10.910 --> 00:22:13.240
Yeah, it's a good disguise.

00:22:13.240 --> 00:22:17.480
Nobody would think you're 
actually a scary witch

00:22:17.480 --> 00:22:19.370
who could flatten a village.

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:21.720
What?

00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:28.410
What's going on? Three girls, 
somewhere like this?

00:22:28.410 --> 00:22:30.190
I guess one of them's a kid.

00:22:30.190 --> 00:22:31.700
She's so pretty!

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:34.010
Why not have a drink?

00:22:34.010 --> 00:22:35.120
I refuse.

00:22:37.000 --> 00:22:38.310
Hey, you drunk—

00:22:38.310 --> 00:22:39.420
What is it, kid?

00:22:39.780 --> 00:22:43.710
You really think kids should 
be in a place like this—

00:22:44.920 --> 00:22:46.370
What the hell?

00:22:47.330 --> 00:22:48.620
That's the price...

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:53.680
For staining my comrade's new clothes.

00:22:54.790 --> 00:22:55.850
<i>Comrade...</i>

00:22:58.740 --> 00:23:03.150
<i>Mistress, this city and the human world</i>

00:23:03.600 --> 00:23:07.070
<i>are so very vulgar and foolish.</i>

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:10.180
Girls...

00:23:12.740 --> 00:23:13.910
<i>It's ugly.</i>

00:23:14.370 --> 00:23:15.630
Not bad.

00:23:16.860 --> 00:23:18.410
<i>But, mistress...</i>

00:23:20.070 --> 00:23:23.300
<i>Even with all that, I can smile!</i>

00:23:32.940 --> 00:23:35.910
<i>If you would continue your journey,</i>

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:41.820
<i>you will see the Apostles again, soon.</i>

00:23:43.070 --> 00:23:47.780
<i>And when that happens, 
their leader will most likely be</i>

00:23:48.190 --> 00:23:49.240
<i>the hawk.</i>
